<article class="env-lemma" id="0949">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0949">Lemma <span data-tag="0949">13.33.7</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $L_ n^\bullet $ be a system of complexes of $\mathcal{A}$. Assume colimits over $\mathbf{N}$ exist and are exact in $\mathcal{A}$. Then the termwise colimit $L^\bullet = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits L_ n^\bullet $ is a homotopy colimit of the system in $D(\mathcal{A})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have an exact sequence of complexes 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \bigoplus L_ n^\bullet \to \bigoplus L_ n^\bullet \to L^\bullet \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Lemma <a href="/tag/093W" data-tag="093W">13.33.6</a>. The direct sums are direct sums in $D(\mathcal{A})$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0A5L" data-tag="0A5L">13.33.5</a>. Thus the result follows from the definition of derived colimits in Definition <a href="/tag/090Z" data-tag="090Z">13.33.1</a> and the fact that a short exact sequence of complexes gives a distinguished triangle (Lemma <a href="/tag/0152" data-tag="0152">13.12.1</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>